            <ArticleTitle>Functional heme oxygenase-1 promoter polymorphism in relation to heart failure and cardiac transplantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>493-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We investigated the functional promoter repeat polymorphism (GT)(n) in the oxidative stress-induced enzyme heme oxygenase-1 in relation to heart failure and complications after transplantation. No influence of the polymorphism on the development of heart failure, graft survival, acute rejection, or transplant atherosclerosis was found.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
